# Optional. If set, step 2 skips wallet resolution and sign-up and uses this key;
# step 3 requires a key. Step 2 does not read or create .agent-wallet.json on this path.
# BLOCKVECTRA_API_KEY=rgw_...

# Optional, step 2 only: private key (0x-prefixed, 32 bytes) of a wallet used for sign-in.
# If set, it takes precedence over .agent-wallet.json and the file is not read or changed.
# Keep it in your local environment only: never commit it, put it in argv, or use a wallet
# that holds funds or is used elsewhere.
#
# If omitted and no API key is set, the first run creates a dedicated login wallet in .agent-wallet.json as
# plaintext JSON (mode 0600, ignored by *wallet*.json); later runs in the same directory
# reuse that wallet and account. Each run without BLOCKVECTRA_API_KEY still creates a new
# server-side API key, and this starter does not revoke it automatically.
# WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...
